# Same question as -33.play, corrected: RAID needs a size/difficulty screen
# tapped through before class:* targets exist (my first attempt skipped it
# and only proved home has no class controls, not the actual question).
# src/input.ts sets menuRequested on Escape *or* p unconditionally, but only
# the fight screen's own update loop ever reads it -- the escape version of
# this bug is already held in direction.md/queued as an issue. This checks
# whether the undocumented `p` binding shares the exact same silent-first-
# PULL defect (same mechanism predicts yes, since the listener does not
# distinguish which key set the flag).
open
tap settings
key p
tap back
tap raid
targets
tap next
targets
tap class:mage:frost
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot after-pull

# Confirm recovery matches the escape report: a second press on the same
# stuck screen should work normally this time.
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot second-attempt
